{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/766", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Summarize this in three sentences: Three girls walk to school together every day. One has blonde hair, and two are brunettes. They all have pink backpacks. Their names are Sarah, Heather, and Nicole.\\nSarah-\\npink backpack, blonde hair.\\nHeather-\\nPink backpack, brown hair.\\nNicole-\\nPink backpack, ______.\", \"response\": \"Nicole has brown hair like the other two girls. All three girls have pink backpacks and they walk to school together every day. Although Sarah has blonde hair, she and the other two girls have brown hair.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/848", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Rewrite this like a 10-year-old wrote it for school. Misspell at least 5 words that a 10-year-old might misspell in their writing. Then, create 3 comprehension questions that a teacher might write to inspire a student to create that work of writing. \\n\\nReference Text: On March 6, 2020, the COVID-19 pandemic arrived in Colombia, bringing with it a new tragedy for Betsiré. Schools closed, and she lost her job. With two mouths to feed, she had no time to lose. She looked everywhere for help and found the Citizen Care Network, a platform created by IDPAC, an entity attached to the Mayor of Bogotá´s Office, that encourages community participation and care for and the most vulnerable populations. To receive support, the person seeking help writes about their situation, and the citizens can choose whom to help. This is how Betsiré received a food voucher from an anonymous person that she used to survive for several weeks.\\n\\nShe also obtained a monetary subsidy as part of the Bogotá Caregiver program, an initiative that the Mayor's Office arranged to address the humanitarian emergency caused by COVID-19 that includes various forms of support, from in-kind subsidies, school meals, and care for the elderly, to solidarity leases, public service payments, deferrals in the payment of taxes, and credits.\\n\\n“Social support programs and the strengthening of social cohesion in communities are both essential to meet the needs of people in vulnerable situations,” noted Dr. Gina Tambini, representative of the Pan American Health Organization (PAHO) in Colombia.\\n\\n\\\"When we consider the health of a person, we must think not only about their physical and mental health, but also about the social, economic and cultural conditions in which they live and how these conditions impact their health.\\\" In this way, community support contributes to the health and well-being of the members of a community.\\\"\\n\\nBetsiré is a tireless fighter and her story is a testament to the State’s social programs and the solidarity of Colombians, showing that with help, the most vulnerable of the vulnerable can build a life even during a pandemic. It also reaffirms that people are stronger together, a call made by PAHO in during its Wellness Week 2020 campaign, which encourages communities to support each other to face COVID-19 and its impact on mental health, while leaving no one behind.\", \"response\": \"When the pandemic came here to Colombia in March 2020, it was bad for me and my family. My mother, who is named Betsiré, lost her job when the schools closed because she worked at my school. We walked with her and looked all over our city for help because we were hungry, and then we found some information at the mayor’s office about the Citizen Care Network.\\n\\nI love the help the Citizen Care Network gave us because there were other people in my comunity who were doing nice things to help families like mine during the pandemic when evereone was losing jobs. We got to meet other families who had kids to play with, and the grone ups would play games with us and tell us it was okay to share our feelings, and they would try to make us less sad.\\n\\nI think my mother is a fiter for always beleving in us and for always trying to help us. We knew she was reallllllly tired, but the nice people in our comunity all worked together like one big family and helped us feel better.\\n\\n1.  What was your experience during the pandemic?\\n2.  How did the pandemic affect your family?\\n3.  What was one thing that made your life better during the pandemic?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/273", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I want to make a cell of excel\\n Calculate the number of Link words in column H, and at the same time, the text in column C must be the same as K6\\n \\n\\n Please give me the formula for the cell\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\n=SUM(H2:H) & \\\" \\\" & IF(C2:C=\\\"K6\\\", \\\"Link\\\", \\\"No Link\\\")\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nSome errors occurred, please confirm again\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, I think the problem is that the formula is trying to reference cells C2:C, which doesn’t exist, because the formula is in cell C1. Please try typing the formula in cell H1 instead.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat is mean about C2:C\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’m sorry, I think I misunderstood your question. If you can give me more information about what you want to do, I’ll try to help.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nI want to make an excel cell\\n The first condition is that the text in column C must be the same as K6\\n If they are the same, then determine the number of Link words in the corresponding seat of column H\\n \\n\\n Please give me the formula of the cell\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\n=IF(C=\\\"K6\\\",SUM(H2:H),0) & \\\" \\\" & IF(C=\\\"K6\\\", \\\"Link\\\", \\\"No Link\\\")\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nshow as #overflow\\n How can I solve it?\", \"response\": \"The \\\"#overflow\\\" error in Excel usually occurs when a formula or function returns a value that is too large to be represented in the cell's format. This can happen when you are trying to perform calculations that result in a very large number or when you are trying to display text that is too long for the cell.\\n \\n\\n To solve this problem, you can try the following solutions:\\n \\n\\n 1. Change the cell format to a larger number format or a longer text format. You can do this by right-clicking on the cell and selecting \\\"Format Cells\\\" from the context menu. In the Format Cells dialog box, select the appropriate format from the list.\\n \\n\\n 2. Use a different formula or function that returns a smaller value. You can also try simplifying the formula by removing unnecessary calculations or functions.\\n \\n\\n 3. Split the formula or function into multiple cells. If the formula is too complex to fit in a single cell, you can split it into multiple cells by breaking it down into smaller parts.\\n \\n\\n 4. Use a macro to perform the calculation. If the formula is very complex and cannot be simplified, you can create a macro to perform the calculation for you. This can be done by recording a macro while you perform the calculation and then editing the macro code to perform the calculation automatically.\\n \\n\\n I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any other questions.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
